# ==================== local/ — everything that does NOT belong on GitHub ====================
#
# One folder for all the working material, so the repo root stays readable and
# there is one rule to remember instead of a growing list of one-off patterns.
#
#   local/NEXT-SESSION.md  the session plan — moved here at his request, it is a
#                          private working note, not part of the project
#   local/commits/     commit messages for `git commit -F` (they do not fit the
#                      CodeAssist box, so they live in a file)
#   local/crashlogs/   crash reports pulled off the device
#   local/logs/        captured packet logs and layout reports
#   local/notes/       internal MDs GitHub does not need (HANDOFF, GRADLE-EXPORT,
#                      the gesture-capture brief, open questions)
#   local/svgs/        the source SVGs the three wear icons were traced from
#
# IGNORED WHOLE, not file by file: a new file dropped into any of these is ignored
# automatically, which is the point. Do not add narrower patterns below — if
# something must be shared, it belongs at the repo root with the other public docs.
#
# WHAT DELIBERATELY STAYS TRACKED at the root: README.md, PROTOCOL.md, CREDITS.md,
# ROADMAP.md and LICENSE. Everything in local/ is working material — including the
# handover plan, which is written for whoever picks the work up next, not for GitHub.
local/